<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose nine points to 1,274.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose nine points to 1,274.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,274 today from 1,265 on June 16, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1349    12.244	  1340    12.169</p>
<p>   1a   1273  9644.000	  1269  9613.000</p>
<p>   2    1503    21.469	  1496    21.375</p>
<p>   2a   1465 12013.000	  1428 11713.000</p>
<p>   3    1326    12.238	  1324    12.219</p>
<p>   3a   1196  9438.000	  1170  9231.000</p>
<p>   6    1281    13.213	  1281    13.213</p>
<p>   7    1196     5.825	  1201     5.850</p>
<p>   8     815     8.963	   812     8.925</p>
<p>   9     730  6381.000	   728  6363.000</p>
<p>  10    1158     5.850	  1161     5.863</p>
